From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 04:52:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-302: IQ2_S gather body arms (opt-in
 GGML_ARIFI_IQ2S_BODY) + ISA dump under GGML_VK_PIPELINE_STATS

Route A lever 3 of lane 302. mul_mat_vec_iq2_s.comp gains spec constant 3, set only on the idg (expert-gather)
pipeline:
- 1 = signs applied to the packed grid bytes as int8 ((g ^ 0xFF) + 1 = -g per byte, g in {8,25,43}, no carry
  crosses a byte), then one int8 convert per weight. float(int8(-g)) == -float(g) exactly and the fma chain is
  unchanged, so the result is byte-identical by construction (the harness checks it). Desk SPIR-V: -16 OpSelect,
  -16 OpFNegate, +10 integer ops per body.
- 2 = DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: skips the 8 KB iq2s grid copy into LDS (wrong values). Prices the per-workgroup init.
- 3 = PLANTED WRONG arm 1 (sign nibbles swapped), test only: the op gate's body-specific RED.
Default 0 = legacy body, unchanged.

ggml-vulkan.cpp: pipelines whose name matches GGML_VK_PIPELINE_STATS are also created with
eCaptureInternalRepresentationsKHR, and their internal representations are printed to stderr (ISA on AMD,
ASSUMED until the first dump). Startup notice adds "iq2_s body N".

Lane: lane-302

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 0fc8010c8730c0319413f46e623b6dcf0f11d297)

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - fork-authored (lane-302); no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - no served number for this commit in the release ledger or the commit message
